{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And it was from when, etc.</b> He mentioned three kinds of authority that he gave him, one after the next. For 'from when' — that is, at the beginning of his success when the Shekhinah cleaved to him, and the success was in the handiwork of Joseph alone — at that time he appointed him over his house, but not over his household, for he had not yet given him authority over all the members of his household; rather, he was an overseer in his house over the work of his own hands. Still more: when his master saw that the success extended from him to himself, so that YHWH was with him along with the master — then he made him overseer over all that he had, and this is the second stage. And regarding the third stage he said, ״וַיְבָרֶךְ ה׳ אֶת בֵּית הַמִּצְרִי בִּגְלַל יוֹסֵף וַיְהִי בִּרְכַּת ה׳ בְּכָל אֲשֶׁר יֶשׁ לוֹ בַּבַּיִת וּבַשָּׂדֶה״ (Genesis 39:5) — and beforehand it was not in the field but only in the house. Therefore ״וַיַּעֲזֹב כָּל אֲשֶׁר לוֹ בְיַד יוֹסֵף״ etc. (Genesis 39:6). And concerning this third stage he had already said ״וַיַּפְקִדֵהוּ עַל בֵּיתוֹ״ (Genesis 39:4) — that he gave him authority over them all." "Another matter: <b>And he was in the house of his master, the Egyptian.</b> His way had been to dwell in tents, for every successful man has many friends and his way is to go to feasts and celebrations. But on account of the distress of his father he did not go here and there, and he was constantly in the house of his master and did not go after the company of his friends. Therefore his master appointed him over his house, and even though he was in his house, HaShem blessed wherever his foot stepped, even what was in the field, even though his feet did not tread there. And when he saw the greatness of his success, therefore ״וַיַּעֲזֹב כָּל אֲשֶׁר לוֹ בְיַד יוֹסֵף״."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "The Kli Yakar traces three escalating stages of Joseph's authority and the blessing upon Potiphar's household, correlating each with the sequence of verses in Genesis 39.", 1 "The phrase 'דַּרְכּוֹ לִהְיוֹת יוֹשֵׁב אֹהָלִים' ('his way had been to dwell in tents') evokes the tribal-pastoral life of Jacob's family; here applied to Joseph's prior social habits."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:33.834793069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}